WEBVTT

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.890
Shark Knight?

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.920
Wasn't that lucky.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.360
We were on an overseas business trip
for public relations.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.650
...Then we happened to stop by a diner...

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.650
...and ran into you guys!...

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.910
Are you all right?

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.900
...Yes, it's just a scratch...

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.400
You two really saved us.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.910
Hopefully it doesn't get infected.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.420
Thanks, Natcchi!

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.020
Don't you know it's illegal to use
magic outside your home country?

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.480
...I didn't have time to think, so...

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.230
Well, I assume that Canada's article 10 of the
magic-prohibition law would apply to this case,

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.430
but if something were to go wrong,
we'll be your witnesses.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.440
Thank you very much.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.280
Are you sure you want to get off here?

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.190
We can take you to a
nearby station if you want.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.760
It's fine. I'll figure out the rest myself.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.450
You'd better become a wizard barrister!

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.840
Here's our cards.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.450
If we're not busy, then we'd
be more than happy to talk.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.710
Okay, I'll study real hard and
become a wizard barrister one day.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.790
Bye!

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.730
...Hm... That girl...

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.720
There were times when I
thought she wanted to kill us.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.730
It was weird.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.990
You're much weirder.
And a pervert. What a joke.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.990
What are you doing, you pervy frog?

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.990
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.990
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:51.290
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:51.290
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.760
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.760
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.750
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.750
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.050
but in the present?

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.050
erabareta ima

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.410
The scales of justice are fragile

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.410
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.470
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.470
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.370
the color of blood

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.370
chi no iro no hana

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.870
I will give all I have

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.870
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.570
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.570
subete wo sasageyou

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.850
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.850
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.700
which I will show the world

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.700
kaze ni hanatte

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.700
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.700
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.370
and look at a new world

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.370
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.020
My love stabs at the cracks

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.020
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.510
of a stagnant fate

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.510
omoi wa nejikonde

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.390
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.390
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.000
time itself will not stop breathing

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.000
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.760
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.760
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.230
and further destruction?

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.230
nani ga nokoru darou

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.960
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.960
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.100
and to the system of the world

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.100
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.770
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.770
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:08.010
even if only ashes will remain

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:08.010
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.120
Let's go swimming!

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.780
It may be hot, but isn't it
too early to go swimming?

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.130
Don't worry about it!
We <i>are in America, after all.</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:24.760
With this nice body, I'll be sure to
have some foreign guys on lock. Bam!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.760
Case 8

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.760
Saint Christopher Charm

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.880
Could you stop being such
...a pervert in front of Diana...

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.260
You never change, Sasorin.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.000
Why would I?

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.020
Hachimitsu, try not to get too excited.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.150
Even I have the right to choose.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.460
Oh, apparently Cecil and Hotaru
made it safely to Canada.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.150
Oh, that's good.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:48.160
W-Wait, they ran into Geah Grim,
and Hotaru used her magic?!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.500
They got into an incident?!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.000
I wouldn't expect
Hotarin to use her magic.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.160
Are they okay?

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.380
Yeah. It doesn't seem to
have turned into any problem.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.170
...Now it's Hotaru...

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.760
Yay, I'm home!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.770
What on Earth?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.180
It's huge!

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.770
It was planted when I was born.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.130
It grew this much
in just seventeen years?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.740
Don't move.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.840
Slowly raise your hands.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:40.880
Don't try anything funny.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.750
If you resist, I'll shoot.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:46.220
Now turn this way.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.630
Daddy!

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.640
Cecil!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.880
Daddy!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.040
It's been so long!

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.600
How've you been?

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.610
I apologize for the mess.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.610
...I didn't expect to see you, Cecil...

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.370
You should've at least called.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.620
I wanted to surprise you.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.620
I didn't expect you to
pull out a rifle, though.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.260
Sorry, sorry.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.880
I'm really sorry about that.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.140
N-No, it's fine.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:25.950
I was using the fortunetelling
tarot cards before you got here.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:30.930
It said I would have some
uninvited guests, and to be wary.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.930
It's rare for your reading
to be wrong, though.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.060
That's some sloppy reading.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.370
I'm no match for you when it
comes to sloppy, Nana Genie.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.060
Hot!

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.400
Hotaru, thank you
for coming such a long way.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.940
The drive must have been rough.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.620
...Oh, well...

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.780
Huh? Daddy, you're out of maple syrup.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:55.750
Yeah, it's been a while
...since I've been home, so...

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.780
...Oh, come on...

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.000
I'll go buy some.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.580
Huh? Hey, wait!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.440
I'll be right back!
Just wait here, Natcchi.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.550
It'd be a shame to not have
some maple syrup while in Canada.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.320
You have a lot of photos.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.700
I take photos for a living.

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:22.260
Taking scenic photos and pictures
for magazines puts food on my table.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.310
I see.

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:28.320
You're the first friend
Cecil's brought home.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.060
Huh?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:34.560
When she was a kid,
she spent most of her time alone.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.870
People were scared
because she was a Wud.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.500
And she was bullied
because she was half Japanese.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.540
They're still a bit
behind on the times in the sticks.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:47.740
I know it's biased to say as her father,

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.880
but I think she's grown up to be
a cheerful girl, despite everything.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.390
I heard about her mother.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:58.390
Did you also hear why she decided
to become a wizard barrister?

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.050
I wanted to go to Japan too,

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:09.670
but Megumi insisted I stay in
Canada and continue my work.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.660
Hotaru, please continue
being Cecil's friend.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.420
She still has a ways to go,
so I'd like you to help her.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:22.160
...All right. If there's anything I can do...

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.760
...It's just, um...

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:29.920
If it's not too much to ask,
could you tell me about the incident?

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.220
...Well...

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.460
I told you not to drop it!

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.760
Don't make me hold everything!

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.970
We're back!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:44.620
We ended up buying a whole bunch
of stuff, so I'll make some lunch!

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:47.420
Do you plan to hospitalize them?

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.860
How rude!

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.450
Man, it's freezing
...and there's no one here...

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.550
Oh, my god!

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:03.750
At least we can start
working on our tans, Sasorin.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.240
You're quite the workaholic.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.510
How admirable.
...On the other hand, my associates...

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.230
Hachimitsu, have a look!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.890
I just had to respond to
an important business email.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.650
No!

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:19.210
Come on, come on!

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.220
Why don't we have some lunch?

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.220
Why don't you take that off?

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.110
This room was kept pretty neat.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.860
Yeah.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.490
Who's this boy?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:41.280
...He was my first crush...
A classmate of mine.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.180
He was my first friend in Japan,

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.840
...so I sent a picture to my dad, but...

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:51.500
"But"?

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.770
I don't think we'll
ever see each other again.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.600
So we're just former friends.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.850
I feel like there's more to it.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.600
Your parents really care about you.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.230
Huh?

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:08.730
I guess.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.860
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.760
...About your mother's incident...

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.360
What exactly happened?

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:18.460
I don't remember at all.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.110
What?

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.560
My memory's spotty.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.820
I don't remember what happened,

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.120
...or why my mom protected me...

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:30.600
I asked my parents before,
but they won't tell me.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:34.240
All they say is that, in order to
protect me, she killed someone.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.880
The trial was awful too.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.880
Even though she said it was self-defense,

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.390
no one believed her.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.340
And because I couldn't
remember anything,

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:46.890
my statements weren't introduced
as evidence. I felt terrible at the time.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:50.770
Food's ready!

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:52.490
'kay!

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.770
Let's go, Natcchi.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.280
When Cecil first awakened,
it was quite the ordeal.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.240
I bought a brand new car with the
money from my first photo collection,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.280
and she immediately
turned it into a diaboloid.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.040
I can see that happening.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.680
...I cried...

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:10.080
I don't blame you.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.540
You're talking about that again?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.920
But Cecil has had a lot
more awakenings lately.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.420
...Yeah...

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.420
Generally, wizards only
have one magical power.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:23.050
I don't know why, either.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:25.760
Daddy?

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:29.660
I might be too late in saying this,
but the use of magic is illegal.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:32.270
Don't forget that you're
a wizard barrister, all right?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.200
Yeah, I know!

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:40.740
Is this a restaurant?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.720
Yes.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:45.280
The interior is a bit unique, but I
promise that their food is delicious.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:47.160
But there aren't any customers.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.410
Did you rent out the place?

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.160
Yes. It's just us here.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.180
H-Huh?

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.260
One more try! I can do it!

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:12.180
That's enough. Here, give them to me.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.690
It's so nice.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.180
I'm glad.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.190
Try to enjoy Canada's nature
to the fullest, since you're here.

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:25.920
Did you forget that I was
forced to come with you?

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:27.720
Oh, yeah.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:29.520
Hey.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:30.600
What?

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:34.210
...Well, about your mother's incident...

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:36.210
Yeah?

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:40.960
If there's a lot of research to do,
I don't mind helping you out.

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:41.960
Huh?

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:46.360
I'm s-saying that I wouldn't
mind helping out a little!

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.470
Only when I'm not busy, though!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:52.740
I'm just curious because I'm a wizard barrister,
so don't get any wrong ideas!

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:54.980
All right. Thanks, Natcchi!

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.110
Wh-What?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.690
What's going on?!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.940
It won't open!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.570
Diana, why?

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:44.950
What the heck?

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.500
Cecil!

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.290
...A metamoloid...

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:01.010
Is this the uninvited guest that
Daddy's reading was about?

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:09.600
Take this!

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.060
Is everyone okay?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.010
Diana!

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:25.700
Why?

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.710
You people are a nuisance.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.040
...For Macal...

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.040
Macal?

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:38.080
...Labone and Macal...

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.350
Hurry and summon your diaboloid!

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.450
There isn't enough metal to summon it!

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.550
What the hell?

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:16.550
You're a pretty useless boss
when we actually need you!

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:17.870
Let's blow her away.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:18.690
All right!

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.370
<i>Hachimitsu Smash!</i>

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.190
Is Kynt in on this too?

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:44.990
I just used him for the invitation
so that I could kill you.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.790
Thank goodness Cecil
ended up going somewhere else,

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.430
since her magic would have
put me at a disadvantage.

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:53.370
...So Sudou...

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.390
Natcchi!

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.380
I'm fine!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.090
No, Cecil! Don't use your magic anymore!

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.570
...My memories...

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.660
...My memories with my parents...

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.660
Our precious memories!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.010
...I won't forgive you...

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:38.040
I won't forgive you!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.730
<i>Cecil Diaboloid, go!</i>

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.560
No way... Where is all this coming from?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.060
Kaede?

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.060
Kaede?

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:25.290
...Why would you do this...

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:28.150
Answer us, Kaede!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.550
...I'm sure you've already forgotten...

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.570
But the suspects you recently caught
...from the robbery gang, No Face...

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.610
One of them is my father.

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:47.110
...No way...

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:52.180
Did you really think that the
accused don't have families?

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.030
The girls' road trip was fun.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:00.010
I actually got a little emotionally attached,

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.190
despite my grudge against you, Cecil.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:03.720
...Kaede...

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:07.370
...I know that my father was the bad guy...

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:12.450
But he also raised me all by himself.

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:17.320
I know that it's nobody's fault,

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:20.240
but I was just overcome with rage.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:25.980
I couldn't think of anything except the
one responsible for sending my father to jail.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:30.460
...That's when he listened to me...

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.720
"He"?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:35.270
He said Cecil is a
terrible wizard barrister.

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:40.970
He said if I could draw out your dormant magic,
then my father's sentence would be reduced.

00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:45.250
...Draw out my magic...

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:46.920
But why?

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.290
...I don't know the details...

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.770
But apparently, it has to do
with the incident six years ago.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.480
You mean my mom's trial?

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.030
I don't know.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.980
I'm just following his orders.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:03.240
Who is he?!

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.750
...Damn it! There's too much fire...

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.170
...Die...

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.010
For him!

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.380
"Him"?

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.770
Just tell me who he is!

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:24.570
...He's...

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:43.670
...Help me...

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.220
She disappeared!

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:03.910
What a big mouth.
You aren't supposed to tell them yet.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:12.770
Huh?

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.390
Were you just there, Tentou?

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.450
...That paralegal...

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.950
Butterfly Law Offices

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.950
...What on Earth just happened...

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:27.530
I don't know.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.570
But it undoubtedly has
...something to do with you, Cecil...

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:48.970
Apparently, both Diana and Kaede abandoned
their missions partway and disappeared.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:52.470
I'm terribly sorry, Father.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:55.270
Your management is wanting, Shizumu.

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.010
...Butterfly may be on to us...

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:00.980
Let us hasten our plans.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.910
Do we kill her

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:04.980
again?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.990
No need.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:13.810
She's evolving faster than
we could've ever expected.

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:17.390
The time for her to become
...the catalyst draws near...

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.610
We're close to obtaining great power.

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.640
This is from Daddy.

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:28.140
Oh, how nostalgic.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:30.630
He wanted me to give it to you.

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:33.710
We managed to find
this one under all the rubble.

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:37.650
I'm sorry, I couldn't protect our home.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:42.020
It's okay. All that matters
is that you and David are safe.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:43.660
Thank goodness.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:54.090
...It's beautiful...

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:03.730
My magic belongs to nobody else.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:09.270
I... I need to do more research.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:32.580
Tears may drench the skies of my heart,

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:32.580
kokoro no sora ni namida afuretemo

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:40.130
but I still want to behold the blue outside

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:40.130
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:47.720
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:47.720
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:55.140
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:55.140
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.140 --> 00:23:02.540
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.140 --> 00:23:02.540
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:06.360
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:06.360
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:14.820
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:14.820
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:20.030
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:20.030
kono mune mou hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.130
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.130
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:29.460
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:29.460
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:37.550
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:37.550
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
